The silent failure the ledger exists for. Release 2 added `slug`, which may
hold NULL, filled by an @from. Release 3 deleted the line, saying every
database had finished release 2 (`@oldest 2`), while production was still
at release 1. Without the ledger, `slug` would be made empty there; with
it, the database is refused. Deploying release 2 first, then 3, fills it.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'Pea Soup');
PRAGMA user_version = 1;

== after
-- @release 3
-- @oldest 2
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, slug TEXT) STRICT;

== after
-- @release 2
-- @from 2 column dish slug = lower(replace(name, ' ', '-'))
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, slug TEXT) STRICT;

== after
-- @release 3
-- @oldest 2
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, slug TEXT) STRICT;

== plan
-- after 1
-- after 2
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `dish`: aside, to make it anew
    ALTER TABLE "dish" RENAME TO "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, slug TEXT) STRICT
  table `dish`: its rows, by id, name, slug = lower(replace(name, ' ', '-'))
    INSERT INTO "dish" ("id", "name", "slug") SELECT "id", "name", (
    lower(replace(name, ' ', '-'))
    ) FROM "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_dish"
migrated from release 1
-- after 3
migrated from release 2

== error
-- after 1
the database is at release 1, before `-- @oldest 2`: the @drop and @from lines it needs were deleted. Open it first with an executable of a release that still had them, or put them back.

== query
SELECT id, name, slug FROM dish

== rows
1 | Pea Soup | pea-soup
